  "body": "  The ring is a complete uniform nonnoetherian Tate -algebra and an integral domain. Moreover,    Lean (isClosed_jetSupport)  Lean (isTateRing_JetA)  Lean (finiteJet_isUniform_of_dvr)  Lean (isPowerBounded_JetA_iff)  Lean (finiteJet_isDomain)  Lean (finiteJet_not_noetherian)   The Gauss norm on is multiplicative, and the restricted Gauss norm on is therefore multiplicative as well. In particular, is a domain, and hence so is its subring . The conditions on the constant and linear -coefficients which define are closed conditions in , so is complete. The image of in is a topologically nilpotent unit, and therefore is a Tate ring.  The coefficient description of shows that it is exactly the unit ball for the restricted Gauss norm on . Since this norm is multiplicative, It follows that is power-bounded if and only if . Thus , and the unit ball is bounded, so is uniform.  For nonnoetherianity, let . If were generated by , then, for every , comparison of the -coefficient in an expression would express as a -linear combination of the -coefficients of the . This would make a finite -module, which is impossible: a finite algebra is integral, whereas a monic equation for , after multiplication by a power of , would put in the proper ideal . Thus is not finitely generated, and is not noetherian.   "
