  "body": " Small perturbation lemma   Let be a complete nonarchimedean normed commutative ring, let be a plus ring containing the closed unit ball , and let satisfy Let be a rational datum with entries in . Write and for . Suppose that for some there are with Let satisfy and write . Then is a rational datum, and define the same rational subset of , and their completed rational localisations are bicontinuously isomorphic by an isomorphism commuting with the canonical maps from .   Lean (datum_isRational)  Lean (rationalOpen_datum)  Lean (equiv)  Lean (equiv_continuous)  Lean (equiv_symm_continuous)  Lean (equiv_canonicalMap)   The scaling hypothesis and the fact that is a unit give with . Hence Since , the element is a unit with inverse in . Multiplying the by this inverse gives a unit-ball Bezout relation for the primed datum; in particular, is rational.  Let lie in the rational subset defined by . Since , relation gives The perturbations have value at most , so and . This proves one inclusion of rational subsets. Applying the same argument to the primed Bezout relation proves the reverse inclusion.  Rational localisation is independent of the datum used to present a rational subset. The equality of the two subsets therefore gives restriction maps in both directions between and . Transitivity of rational restriction shows that their composites are the identity. The two restriction maps are continuous and commute with the canonical maps from , as required.   "
