{
  "id": "rem-second-example-relation",
  "level": "2",
  "url": "#rem-second-example-relation",
  "type": "Remark",
  "number": "7.11",
  "title": "Relation with the first construction.",
  "body": " Relation with the first construction   The finite-jet and weighted-parity examples use different mechanisms. In the finite-jet ring, a whole tail becomes infinitely -divisible and the bad chart acquires a nilpotent. In the weighted-parity ring, every rational calculation can be moved into a noetherian finite head and then carried coefficientwise through a -tail. Its bad chart remains a domain, and nonuniformity is witnessed by the unbounded family of nonnilpotent power-bounded elements. The use of an infinite monomial support and of unbounded power-bounded directions is in the tradition of the examples of Buzzard Verberkmoes and Mihara; the finite-head coefficientwise descent is the additional feature that makes sheafiness accessible here.   "
}
